WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:00.710
Thank you.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:30.620
Thank you.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:01.190
Thank you.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:46.600
I've got a little money to bet on this ride, men.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.600
What horse is Tom riding?

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:49.220
Dynamite.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.040
Dynamite?

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.220
I'll take $10 on that horse.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:52.980
$10 on the horse?

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:53.300
Bet.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.770
I'll take $5 on the horse.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.210
I'll take $10 on Tom.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:57.850
All right, men.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.430
I'll put my motor on the horse.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:01:59.930
On the horse.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.310
You want to come up here? You want to make a little bet, men?

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.530
All right, come on over there, fellas, and give me a little bet here on this ride.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.760
Tell him I've got to pay you.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:57.920
Where's mine?

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.180
Well, you better on the horse.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:02:59.660
Get out of here.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.760
Well, you sure made a cowboy ride, Tom.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.320
Here's your winnings.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:07.810
My winnings?

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:08.350
Sure.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.420
I bet our bankroll on you.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:12.840
Thanks, Wendy.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.460
Tom, what are you going to do with all your money?

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.360
I don't know.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.360
I'll bet I know.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.200
You're going home to see your dad for a spell.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:22.800
No, Wendy.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.070
The last quarrel I had with dad was enough.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.400
I'm not going back until he sends for me.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.280
Well, how about Nancy?

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.220
Ain't you going to see her?

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:33.190
Next time I see Nancy will be when I've saved enough cash to get married.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.230
We can buy a little ranch of our own.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.710
Attaboy, Tom. That's the way I like to hear you talk.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.570
Well, see, boys. The last man in town buys a drink.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:07.300
Come in.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:14.980
What's wrong, Scarface?

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.740
Mr. Duncan, I just came in from the north end of the ranch,

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.350
and Taps Smiley's men had already had three sides of that spring

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:22.690
fenced in when I got there.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.090
Did his men tell you it was Smiley's orders?

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:25.920
Yes, sir.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.060
That Smiley rode up and said it was all right

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.960
since you and he had decided to join ranch.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.060
Did you join ranches?

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:37.700
We talked about it, but nothing is signed, and I don't stand for Smiley fencing in any

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:38.480
of my property.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.060
Well, I stopped him anyway.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.960
Smiley's kind of sore, but I told him that I didn't know anything about your private

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:44.340
business.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:45.800
You did right, Scarface.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:47.920
See you in the morning.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.380
I'll have the payroll ready for you, then.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:51.840
Good night, Mr. Don.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:52.460
Good night.

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:57.860
Oh, hello, Mr. Heideker.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.280
I didn't hear you come up on the porch.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:04:59.980
Yeah, hold on.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.840
this. I had my little boots on, that's why I spoke. The boss in? Yeah, he's over that

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:21.870
to dance. Oh, yeah. Thanks. Well, I'm glad to see you looking so well, John. Well, my

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:26.650
foot, shot full of rheumatism, hardly able to walk, and a peck of trouble besides. Come

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:26.690
a'.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.510
Here's the $5,000 cash you wanted.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.140
Just as good as gold.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.020
Anyway, better not to let it lie in the bank.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.460
You know, you must have a good deal of cash on hand now, John.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.790
Wouldn't you like to know?

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:49.870
Well, here's the final draft of your will.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:51.750
Short and to the point.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:53.900
Just what I wanted.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.230
Only one question.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:55.760
Shoot.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.710
How will that affect Smiley in case I go partnership with him?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.580
Well, naturally, if you sign a partnership agreement, he'd be entitled to half of your estate.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.230
And the cash, too?

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:10.700
Oh, no, not the cash, so long as you don't happen to have a joint bank account.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:11.290
Oh.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.780
Nobody but Tom will ever know where to find the cash.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.560
When do you expect Tom back?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.540
I wrote him two weeks ago.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:22.060
He ought to be here now.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.550
Maybe he was out on the rain.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:35.140
Rusty's the only one that understands me, and it don't talk back.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:40.360
Well, do you want me to draw up that partnership agreement for you and Taps, Marley?

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:45.560
No, no. Not now. I won't sign nothing until Tom gets you back.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:54.880
Well, all right, John. You're the boss. I'll file the will.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.470
And you let me know when you get ready for the partnership.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:06:59.370
All right.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.180
Hope Tom gets back soon.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:02.900
Goodbye, John.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:03.690
Good night.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.060
Sure is raining.

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.090
Well, good night.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:16.280
Good night.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:03.460
Thank you.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:55.110
Again, hey?

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.110
Come on.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.360
Yeah.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:30.980
What are you doing here?

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:32.660
What do you think?

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:34.570
Nothing.

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:37.020
Liquor's pretty wet.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:39.510
Dropping a lot of water.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:42.780
Might make a pool on the floor.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:43.920
I just got here.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:45.900
I want to find out about our agreement.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:47.390
What agreement?

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.860
Oh, don't be silly.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:50.800
You know what I mean.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:55.640
Our agreement to consolidate the Duncan and Smiley ranches in one.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:57.210
Now, how about it?

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.670
Nothing doing that.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:10:59.820
Why?

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.380
I won't do anything until Tom gets here.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.020
What do you care about Tom?

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.380
You quarrel with him, send him away.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.190
Now you're going to wait until he gets back?

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.210
Yes, I am.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:10.550
What's he to you?

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.560
He always antagonized you.

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:14.910
You and he never could agree about anything.

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.560
No matter what quarrels we've had, he's my son.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.280
And I love him as my son.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:21.210
Is that clear?

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:23.600
Oh, that's clear enough.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.480
But Tom's a harm's carom, young fella.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.300
He never could protect your interests like I could.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.960
Well, maybe not.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.310
But just the same, I'll take a chance on my own face and blood.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:38.180
Well, I don't blame you for sticking up for Tom, but just the same...

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:39.060
Just the same what?

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.710
I ain't good to have him around sparking my daughter Nancy, if you get what I mean.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:47.490
So you think my son ain't good enough for your daughter, eh?

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:48.710
That's what I mean.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.850
Get out of my house, Kepp Smiley.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:53.800
I never want to see you again.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:57.220
My son is better than your whole tribe.

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:58.680
Well, get out of here!

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:17.130
what do you want? Oh, nothing. I heard a commotion. I thought something was wrong. Something is wrong.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:23.240
Somebody's snooping around. I wish you'd keep a close watch on the house night and day. All right,

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.190
Mr. Duncan. Good night. Good night.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:58.010
When they get back in the line.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.360
Hey, right from here, huh?

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:01.960
Right from there.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.640
Hey, wait a minute.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.310
I'll bet you the drink will miss the whole board.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:07.610
That's a bet.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:08.810
What'll it be, whiskey?

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:09.470
Sure.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:10.330
Okay.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:20.220
Hey, Wendy.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.620
That'll cost you two bucks.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.200
All right, Tom, it's your turn.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.520
Let's see how good you are now.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.580
Now, just to show you how easy this is, I'm going to do it with my eyes closed.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:28.960
Yeah?

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:30.860
Ready? Go.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:36.080
Bulldog, look where you landed.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.770
Hey, what's the idea?

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.730
Wait a minute. We got a drink coming on you, partner.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.210
All right. Come on, everybody.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:45.950
Come on, boy.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.010
You nicked me.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.670
Yeah, I'm sorry. I'll throw straighter next time.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:53.550
Come on, boy.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:55.590
Give it up. Give it up.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:56.590
Come on, Bill.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.150
Yeah, come on. Have a night, boy.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:13:59.430
