00:29:09.490 --> 00:29:11.290
Have you any idea where the cash might be hidden?

00:29:11.880 --> 00:29:14.260
No, excepting this note.

00:29:14.990 --> 00:29:17.190
The last thing your father wrote and left unfinished.

00:29:18.270 --> 00:29:19.290
It might be a clue.

00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:20.800
What does it say?

00:29:22.150 --> 00:29:24.810
Dear Tom, I'm at the end of the trail.

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:26.700
My enemies are closing in.

00:29:27.300 --> 00:29:29.860
I have left you the ranch and all the stock in my will.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:33.310
but there is $50,000 cash hidden in the house.

00:29:34.020 --> 00:29:35.440
You will find it if you follow.

00:29:36.440 --> 00:29:37.520
That's as far as he went.

00:29:38.660 --> 00:29:39.860
What do you suppose that means?

00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:44.490
You've got me, Tom, but it must be some clue to the missing cash.

00:29:45.220 --> 00:29:47.520
For my part, I think I've been double-crossed.

00:29:48.990 --> 00:29:49.800
What, Miley?

00:29:50.620 --> 00:29:53.850
Well, you know, Tom, your dad and me was practically partners,

00:29:53.850 --> 00:29:56.580
and I think I ought to have been remembered in the will.

00:29:56.910 --> 00:29:58.350
Have you ever written an agreement to that effect?

00:29:59.070 --> 00:29:59.970
Oh, no, not...

00:30:00.020 --> 00:30:06.360
written sort of a verbal conversation but that's enough for me when I give my

00:30:06.360 --> 00:30:12.320
word it's a deal smiling any rightful claims you put in you can be sure I'll

00:30:12.320 --> 00:30:17.520
straighten out all right but it don't look square to me but smiley come on

00:30:17.520 --> 00:30:28.220
Nancy I'll go get the team

00:30:34.700 --> 00:30:35.780
What's the matter here, Dad, Nancy?

00:30:36.470 --> 00:30:38.490
You know, I'm trying my best to be fair with him.

00:30:39.140 --> 00:30:40.480
Oh, don't blame him, Tom.

00:30:40.930 --> 00:30:41.590
Quick-tempered.

00:30:42.360 --> 00:30:44.220
Good deal like your father used to be.

00:30:45.230 --> 00:30:48.760
I guess, uh, maybe we're just a couple of chips off the old blocks, huh?

00:30:49.660 --> 00:30:56.380
Come on, Nancy.

00:30:56.730 --> 00:30:57.210
We're ready.

00:31:17.820 --> 00:31:22.040
clear now, excepting the cash, which belongs to you, if you can find it.

00:31:22.380 --> 00:31:25.790
Yeah, it's like Wendy and I are going to have to do a little prospecting.

00:31:26.890 --> 00:31:28.390
Okay, I got a keen nose for cash.

00:31:28.960 --> 00:31:29.860
Well, if you need me.

00:31:30.220 --> 00:31:31.220
You know where you can find it.

00:31:37.520 --> 00:31:38.000
Goodbye, Bob.

00:31:38.340 --> 00:31:38.560
Bye.

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:25.640
told me something funny about that note your dad never finished writing you're right wendy

00:32:26.020 --> 00:32:29.640
there's one thing sure the man who killed dad was after the cash

00:32:31.660 --> 00:32:32.500
Let's see that note.

00:32:32.980 --> 00:32:33.440
All right.

00:32:33.960 --> 00:32:34.700
It's there on the table.

00:32:34.880 --> 00:32:47.080
What became of that note?

00:32:47.340 --> 00:32:48.420
Hardiker left it right here.

00:32:48.940 --> 00:32:49.460
That's right.

00:32:50.630 --> 00:32:51.290
Couldn't be here.

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:52.860
Hey!

00:33:02.480 --> 00:33:03.140
Hey

00:33:31.440 --> 00:33:34.740
Say, I haven't smelt that odor since my second wife crowned me with a rolling pin.

00:33:35.630 --> 00:33:38.010
An old sawbones put 16 stitches in my dome.

00:33:38.230 --> 00:33:42.980
Ha ha! I wonder what happened to things.

00:33:48.020 --> 00:33:49.340
You know, and it's a funny thing.

00:33:49.560 --> 00:33:52.320
A fella never misses his dad, so he loses him.

00:33:53.740 --> 00:33:56.020
If I'd have stayed at home, maybe he'd still be here.

00:33:57.440 --> 00:33:57.700
Right.

00:34:05.140 --> 00:34:08.150
Well, the talking ground ain't gonna bring them back, Tom.

00:34:08.700 --> 00:34:10.920
Besides, it's about bedtime. Let's get some shut eyes.

00:34:12.590 --> 00:34:18.880
All right. On the porch.

00:34:32.720 --> 00:34:34.880
You go out the back way, and I'll go the front.

00:35:09.990 --> 00:35:26.820
It's pretty tough, anyway.

00:35:27.590 --> 00:35:29.430
Wendy's gone, just like St. Pat.

00:35:31.630 --> 00:35:34.200
Look here, Tom. I'm going to quit.

00:35:35.380 --> 00:35:36.800
You wouldn't do that, Scarface.

00:35:37.670 --> 00:35:38.790
Oh, yes, I would.

00:35:39.630 --> 00:35:42.150
These goings-on are too much for me.

00:35:42.980 --> 00:35:43.760
Now, listen to me.

00:35:44.480 --> 00:35:46.360
You worked with my dad for 12 years.

00:35:46.900 --> 00:35:48.200
Don't that mean anything to you?

00:35:48.930 --> 00:35:50.090
Yes, it does.

00:35:57.090 --> 00:35:59.700
Well, I'll stick it out with you.

00:36:03.580 --> 00:36:11.060
the cook you're the best ranch foreman in the state what's the matter now more mystery no boy

00:36:11.060 --> 00:36:15.890
your heart's in the right place forget about it let's go to town i gotta tend to dad's will

00:36:15.890 --> 00:36:18.820
you saddle up the horses i'll get the papers okay

00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:30.600
Bye.

00:37:06.490 --> 00:37:07.880
Sure thing, what happened?

00:37:09.810 --> 00:37:11.130
That fella shot me.

00:37:11.920 --> 00:37:12.480
Better get him.

00:37:13.380 --> 00:37:14.220
Will you be all right?

00:37:14.400 --> 00:37:15.640
Never mind me, get him.

00:37:18.510 --> 00:37:19.230
Go get him, Tom.

00:38:28.190 --> 00:38:28.910
He comes now, boys.

00:38:29.470 --> 00:38:29.970
Get ready with this.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:30.220
Let's go.

00:39:06.650 --> 00:39:21.660
Come on, boys, tie him up. Put him on your horse.

00:39:48.010 --> 00:39:56.540
see tom duncan you know i don't want you to see him dad i thought you and i settled fast i'm going

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:00.500
be sorry.

00:40:31.756 --> 00:40:32.616
Get down off of there.

00:40:36.460 --> 00:40:38.840
You boys go on back to town. I'll take care of this fella.

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:40.340
Come on and I'll help.

00:40:52.428 --> 00:40:52.608
Yo.

00:40:52.844 --> 00:40:55.344
Get this guy out and see if he won't get away.

00:40:56.108 --> 00:40:58.128
Don't worry, boss. He'll be safe with me.

00:40:58.476 --> 00:40:59.356
I'm going back.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:01.200
this job long.

00:41:02.364 --> 00:41:02.944
Who's there?

00:41:03.452 --> 00:41:04.072
Forget it.

00:41:05.372 --> 00:41:05.672
All right.

00:42:49.260 --> 00:42:51.260
How'd you feel in my place?

00:42:51.308 --> 00:42:52.588
You said it the first time.

00:42:53.100 --> 00:42:55.520
But don't think for a minute that you can get away with anything.

00:42:56.012 --> 00:42:57.392
I'll pick your word for it, brother.

00:43:00.444 --> 00:43:01.444
You got a smoke?

00:43:01.532 --> 00:43:02.532
Sure.

00:43:04.828 --> 00:43:05.668
I guess I'm out.

00:43:06.716 --> 00:43:08.096
I'd give anything for a cigarette.

00:43:09.820 --> 00:43:11.740
I got a couple of packs of my saddle bag.

00:43:12.124 --> 00:43:12.764
I'll get them.

00:43:13.500 --> 00:43:15.240
But no shenanigans while I'm gone.

00:43:15.480 --> 00:43:16.420
Don't be silly.

00:43:16.860 --> 00:43:17.900
How far can I get?

00:43:54.540 --> 00:43:56.570
something, will you? What am I here for?

00:43:57.030 --> 00:43:57.930
Keep you out of trouble.

00:44:00.570 --> 00:44:02.730
Tell me, who's the fellow in the black cloak?

00:44:03.290 --> 00:44:04.430
Wouldn't you like to know?

00:44:04.610 --> 00:44:05.430
I sure would.

00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:06.960
He shot my foreman.

00:44:07.360 --> 00:44:07.480
Huh.

00:44:08.230 --> 00:44:09.730
Maybe your foreman got in the way.

00:44:11.040 --> 00:44:11.560
I see.

00:44:12.820 --> 00:44:14.200
Then I might get in the way, too.

00:44:15.690 --> 00:44:16.030
Maybe.

00:44:16.800 --> 00:44:18.060
Just make yourself to home.

00:44:18.920 --> 00:44:19.580
Thanks, I will.

00:44:19.740 --> 00:44:29.460
What are you so restless about?

00:44:30.060 --> 00:44:31.300
Just getting a little exercise.

00:44:31.880 --> 00:44:33.300
Can't you get it sitting on a chair?

00:44:35.100 --> 00:44:35.900
I think so.

00:45:24.190 --> 00:45:24.430
Network.

00:45:32.840 --> 00:45:34.350
Hey, you're cheating.

00:45:35.600 --> 00:45:35.740
Huh?

00:45:39.990 --> 00:45:41.410
That ten of clubs right there.

00:47:39.880 --> 00:47:41.220
Give me the sheriff's office, please.

00:47:53.420 --> 00:47:55.130
Sheriff, this is Tom Duncan.

00:47:55.520 --> 00:47:57.040
I wish you'd come over to my place pronto.

00:47:57.650 --> 00:47:59.050
There's something dead wrong over here.

00:48:00.220 --> 00:48:01.040
And please hurry.

00:49:50.124 --> 00:49:51.124
How'd you get out of here?

00:49:51.124 --> 00:49:52.124
I don't through the tap door.

00:49:52.556 --> 00:49:54.616
Wendy and Singer bounding gas right over there.

00:50:08.220 --> 00:50:09.100
Ready? Those men.

00:50:09.340 --> 00:50:10.220
The sheriff is coming.

00:50:11.004 --> 00:50:11.384
Okay.

00:52:22.380 --> 00:52:23.180
Which way does it go?

00:55:30.730 --> 00:55:33.500
Thank you.

00:56:26.684 --> 00:56:28.104
Think it's the man who killed my dad.

00:56:32.876 --> 00:56:34.256
Why, it's Burt Hardicker, the lawyer.

00:56:51.084 --> 00:56:52.084
Romantic?

00:56:52.684 --> 00:56:53.584
I've got a ranch.

00:56:55.020 --> 00:56:56.080
I got some cash.

00:56:57.036 --> 00:56:57.796
Have I got the girl?

00:57:00.220 --> 00:57:01.180
What do you think?

00:57:02.364 --> 00:57:03.124
I ain't faking.
